# What the next device-lab run does. Edit and push to run again.
# (2026-10-25, third: the Original on ExoPlayer. On both real phones (Test
# Lab run 40188289751) every line of the Quality menu passed but Original:
# a move from ExoPlayer to libmpv that held the picture 5.3-6.1 s. Now the
# Original plays on ExoPlayer too, as one MP4 through the proxy ("open file
# (exo)"), libmpv only if ExoPlayer cannot. Sintel, full speed, the jumps
# and the tour. Run 40186513057, the busy 4G line: 17 of 17.)
# (2026-10-25, second: a phone line, not Starlink. The emulator's whole
# link held to 4 Mbit/s down, 2 up, 80-200 ms, 0.5 % loss — a busy
# Myanmar 4G evening —
# and Sintel through the jumps, every line of its Quality menu, the far
# jump's landing picture and the way back from Home. Also in the build: the
# player's messages in the dark pill near the top, and a quality choice
# that waits out a reconnect instead of being refused. Run 40184478393,
# Tears of Steel at full speed: 15 of 15, every menu line taken.)
# (2026-10-25: Tears of Steel, the other open film, because the owner's
# phone said "Could not switch quality" on it in 1.64.74 while Sintel's
# changes all took. The jumps, then every line of its Quality menu in
# turn — Original included — then Auto (LAB check tour->…), with the
# refusal's reason in the trail. Home after 170 s: the tour takes longer.)
# (2026-10-24: the ladder on ExoPlayer — the test film (Sintel) with the
# viewer's jumps: seek, a change of quality, skip, swipe, back to Auto, each
# with how long the picture stood still. flows: jumps, in run.sh.
# Run 40076455852: 5/5 landed, a quality change froze the picture 0.2 s,
# but the 240p picked never showed. Again, with the steering in the trail.
# Run 40079651806: the master had no RESOLUTION, so every rung's height was
# unknown and 240p matched the best rung; Auto trusted one reading and
# stalled after a seek. Again, with both fixed. Run 40092901280: 5/5.)
# (2026-10-24, after 1.64.73: the seek bar's pictures one at a time, the
# newest next — on both real phones (Test Lab 40118247783) a swipe's seven
# pictures queued, the last 1.3-1.5 s late; a far jump shows the picture
# of where it lands until its own frame is drawn (LAB check landing); and
# the grant is asked to run beside the database (x-region), which the
# edge log's region says. The jumps, previews and the way back must pass
# as in run 40116409244.)
# (2026-10-24, 1.64.73 candidate: far jumps land on a keyframe and the
# rungs share one pool of connections — the trail times each jump ("hls
# jump", "exo picture after seek"); the seek bar's preview pictures
# (LAB check preview-*); and away to the home screen and back, which must
# bring the picture back ("exo surface back", "exo picture back").
# Run 40114408831: 8/8, previews 6 KB in 0.9 s / 0 ms held / 0.7 s; but
# the return was made with `am start` (a new intent, not the launcher's)
# and checked nothing. Again: the launcher's way back, and the app counts
# the frames drawn after it ("LAB check back").)
# (2026-10-23: the QR scanner, opened and left running, on the 1.64.70
# candidate — its CameraX and ML Kit were raised for 16 KB memory pages under
# a mobile_scanner built against the old versions. flows/qr_scanner.yaml.)
# (2026-10-16: 1.64.64's fixes again, on a build where every icon button is
# named by its tooltip — then the player's Cut, which now really cuts. In
# that order: a cut run that stops mid-film leaves a "Resume?" snackbar that
# never times out while Maestro's accessibility service runs, and it sat on
# the folder bar's Hide button in run 38841902376. Then again on the build
# that reports a cut without sound and has the 48 dp tap targets. Now the
# exact cut: Media3's smart cut from A, measured with ffprobe after. Run
# 38856111434: the High-profile film fell into Media3's whole-clip
# re-encode; now that is cut short and made lossless (cut), and a Baseline
# film proves the smart cut itself (cut_exact). Run 38867811036: the
# fallback works (cut: cancelled at 20 s, lossless saved); cut_exact was
# cancelled at 12.5 s too, the emulator's all-software video being far
# slower than a phone's, so it now runs alone with a lab-only five-minute
# budget to read Media3's own verdict. Run 38870594057: optimization=6,
# format mismatch: Media3 stitches only when this phone's encoder writes the
# file's parameter sets byte for byte (a video it recorded), so for others
# the exact cut re-encodes the clip. Exact start is now the user's choice,
# with progress and Cancel; the default is the lossless cut, which says
# where it starts.)
#
# The network the emulator is given, as the Android emulator console takes
# it: speed is "up:down" in kbit/s, delay is "min:max" in milliseconds.
# 24000 down is ~3 MB/s — the meter reading reported from Myanmar 4G.
# "full" and "none" leave the line to the long film's own profiles below.
NET_SPEED=full
NET_DELAY=none
# Share of incoming packets dropped on the host (empty = none). What makes a
# single TCP connection slow on a mobile line; see run.sh.
NET_LOSS=
# Which release to install. "latest" or a tag such as v1.64.48-361.
APK_TAG=latest
# Which flows to run, in order (files in flows/). Two-second CMAF fragments.
FLOWS="jumps"
# Rehearse the Test Lab game-loop playback first (1 = yes).
LOOP=0
# (build check for the payment screen's Open KPay channel; hub + title page)
# Resume and More like this, the album; live catalogue)
# A library pushed to the emulator before the flows: this many short videos
# across DCIM/Camera, Download and Movies, a few of them truncated (files a
# thumbnailer cannot open), plus one 60 s 720p film to play. 0 = none.
LIBRARY=12
# "lab" builds this branch for x86_64 and runs it natively (default);
# "release" installs the released arm64 APK (needs ARM translation).
APK_SOURCE=lab
# 1 = three-button navigation and a punch-hole camera, like the owner's phone
# (the player's insets then match the MX screenshots' phone).
PHONE_LIKE_OWNER=1
# Which screen to emulate: pixel_6 (phone) or a tablet such as pixel_c.
EMU_PROFILE=pixel_6
# The emulator's back camera: none, or emulated (a moving test picture) for
# flows/qr_scanner.yaml. flows/qr_no_camera.yaml needs none.
EMU_CAMERA=emulated
# 1 = start the Local Network servers (tool/netlab/servers.sh) on the runner
# for flows/network.yaml; the emulator reaches them at 10.0.2.2.
NETLAB=0
# The stream A/B (flows streamab_N): the lab film is served from the runner behind
# netem — one-way delay, loss on the film's packets, a rate cap — and played
# through the real stream proxy with N connections. Seconds each film plays.
STREAM_NETEM="delay 75ms loss 1% rate 32mbit"
STREAM_SECONDS=60
# MB of the one big file flows/transfer_speed.yaml sends (0 = none).
BIGFILE_MB=0
# THE LONG FILM (flows streamlong_PROFILE_LANES; see run.sh): two and a half
# hours of open films at the ladder's rungs. Each PROFILE_<name> is the file
# to play (long_<it>.mp4: 1080, 720, 1080frag or 720frag — the same films
# as fragmented MP4), then the line: one-way delay (both ways), loss on the
# film's packets, rate cap, and optionally the line's queue in packets
# (default 10000 — at 4 Mbit/s that is half a minute of queue, far more than
# a phone network holds; slowq has one second). Myanmar as measured and
# reported:
#   mm4g   a good 4G evening in town     150 ms round trip, 0.5 % loss, 4 MB/s
#   lossy  4G that drops packets         200 ms, 1 %, 4 MB/s
#   busy   a crowded cell                250 ms, 2 %, 2 MB/s — Auto picks 720p
#   slow   the edge of coverage          300 ms, 1 %, 0.5 MB/s — 720p
PROFILE_mm4g="1080 75ms 0.5% 32mbit"
PROFILE_lossy="1080 100ms 1% 32mbit"
PROFILE_busy="720 125ms 2% 16mbit"
PROFILE_slow="720 150ms 1% 4mbit"
PROFILE_slowq="720 150ms 1% 4mbit 340"
PROFILE_mm4gfrag="1080frag 75ms 0.5% 32mbit"
PROFILE_lossyfrag="1080frag 100ms 1% 32mbit"
PROFILE_busyfrag="720frag 125ms 2% 16mbit"
PROFILE_slowfrag="720frag 150ms 1% 4mbit"
# Seconds played before the first of three jumps (then +20 s, +40 s), and after it.
LONG_SEEK_AFTER=45
LONG_AFTER_SEEK=60

# The climb flow: a catalogue title played through the real API, Worker and
# R2 (Sintel, the free test film), opening small from a seeded link estimate
# (CLIMB_SEED_KBPS) and watched for CLIMB_S seconds.
CLIMB_TITLE=0839dacb-59ae-4c95-9279-4901b925965d
# The jumps flow on another open film (CC-BY); empty for the test film.
JUMPS_TITLE=
JUMPS_AWAY_AFTER=130
JUMPS_S=240
CLIMB_SEED_KBPS=500
CLIMB_S=240
